From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:09:12 +0100
Subject: --version, and GNU-style --help, which help2man can read

"disparPDF --version" and "disparPDFc --version" print the name of the
program that was run, its version, the Qt and Poppler versions built
with, and the license, and exit; like --help, this needs no display.
The version number is now set only in project() in CMakeLists.txt,
which passes it to the code, so that it and aboutform.cpp can no longer
drift apart (5e0ca09 had to bring them back into step).

--help now lists the options in the usual two columns, under headings,
with the result codes of batch mode, and names the program that was run
(disparPDF or disparPDFc), leaving out --batch for disparPDFc, which is
always in batch mode.  Also fixed: "--debug=3 as --debug=3".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
